WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.460
What?!

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.580
Why're you sendin' me 
to that rundown church

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.610
just to teach a bunch of 
brats how to read and write?!

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.370
That's up Sosuke's alley!

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.740
You can forget it!

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.120
In that case, why don't you 
swap jobs with me, Shino?

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.370
What's your job?

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.750
Today I will begin 
exterminating the rats

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.120
in that "rundown" church's 
attic in earnest.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:25.870
Care to trade?

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.880
Hence I'm stuck babysitting for the day.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.830
Hey, just a sec!

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.260
Jeez, you brats!

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.830
Sit your butts down and listen to me!

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.770
Say, you ever been to school?

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.770
No, I haven't.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.270
Are you retarded?

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.440
How're you gonna teach us when

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.550
you haven't been to school yerself?

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.410
We ain't morons just 'cause we're 
from the red-light district!

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.890
This is stupid! Let's go.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:00:59.890
Yeah, let's go!

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.790
Hey! Stop right there!

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.000
They're not my problem.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.510
Blue Bird

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.510
Mr. Shino? Read this!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.350
This kid's eyes...

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.560
Oh! You must mean Kaho.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.580
Supposedly she was born blind.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:07.030
Reverse Flow

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.600
She seems to be fascinated with 
foreign fairytales lately.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.390
I'll hunt one down for you.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.210
Oh, she brought this.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.980
Blue Bird, I see.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:21.300
It seems rather tattered and worn.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.830
A bunch of the pages are missing.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.410
I read it back when I was a kid,

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.310
so I can fill in most 
of the gaps as I go.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.690
Is that right?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:36.050
Still, Kaho generally doesn't 
take well to strangers.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.820
I'm surprised she has 
warmed up to you, Shino.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.560
Don't go there!

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.570
She only likes me 'cause I 
promised to read to her tomorrow.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.460
I'd appreciate it if

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.430
you treated the other children 
with equal kindness.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.570
So like, they aren't enrolled 
in school, are they?

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:56.020
Right.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.590
Why not?

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.090
This lad ain't too bright, is he?

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:07.600
Th-these hags are still 
hard on my heart!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.260
How could a kid born in the 
red-light district without

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.910
a family registry waltz into school?

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.400
You sure are a dumb one!

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.710
And you let the kids get 
away durin' the day!

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.610
You ain't the least bit helpful, runt!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.550
Don't call me a runt!

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.580
Now, now.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.140
I'm certain Kaho is eagerly 
looking forward to tomorrow.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.480
Please do your best to remember what

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.620
happens in the parts where 
the pages are missing.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.030
I am spending the night 
here at the church,

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.590
so please head on back without me.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.130
Like I'm gonna help 
him exterminate rats!

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.070
This stinks.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.230
Guess I'll spend the night at Kona-ya.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.380
Hey! If it isn't the 
kid from the church!

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.890
Long time no see! Wanna drop in?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.530
Uh, nah. I don't have 
any money on me today.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.960
DAIKOKUDO'S PORK BUNS

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:02.510
Aw, the man with the 
wallet ain't with ya?

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.300
You poor dear!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.230
Here!

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.910
Daikoku

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.930
It's a prototype.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.590
I was thinkin' you could test it out.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.020
Wow, you sure?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.290
Yeah, eat up! And tell me whatcha think.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:17.980
Curry?

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.320
Ain't it cool?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.300
Sure. I guess it's good.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.570
Ya don't sound too 
enthusiastic. Was it a dud?

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.180
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.030
I just like my curry 
loaded with goodies.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.140
Sosuke throws in stuff like

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.470
cheese or tops it off with a boiled egg.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.310
Yeah? Cheese and a boiled egg, eh?

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:41.110
And if you're goin' all 
out, make some with

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.750
pork stew or pork kimchee!

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.130
Considering the season, chestnut 
and pumpkin buns would be cool!

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.760
What else?

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:49.950
C'mon! Let's go outside!

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:51.950
Wait!

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.700
Mr. Shino?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.450
"On Christmas Eve,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.720
the brother and sister Tyltyl 
and Mytyl went on a journey."

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.610
"They left to find the 
bluebird of happiness."

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.300
"Along the way, they visited 
the Land of Memory,

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.330
where they saw their 
grandmother and grandfather

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.750
"along with their younger brothers and 
sisters, who had already passed away."

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.840
"'My, we haven't seen you in ages!

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.520
Why don't you come visit more often?'"

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.240
"'We couldn't come if we wanted to.'"

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.280
"'All you have to do is remember us.'"

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.370
"'When you do, it awakens 
us from our slumber.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.750
Then we can visit you.'"

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.300
Wanna try a different book?

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.600
Nuh-uh.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.940
How do you remember someone 
if you don't know their name

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.720
or what they look like?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.270
Can you see someone important 
to you just by remembering them?

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.280
So?

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.890
You're back late.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.480
I'm sorry. Did I wake you up?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.040
I figured you'd spend the 
night at Kona-ya again.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.940
Ya know, I'm really not cut out 
for workin' with these kids.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.750
They ran away from me again today.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.320
Despite that, hasn't Kaho 
taken a real liking to you?

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.500
Kaho, huh?

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.730
"How do you remember someone 
if you don't know their name

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.440
or what they look like?"

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.540
How am I supposed to answer that!

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.430
I've heard that she was

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:52.600
dumped in front of a brothel 
when she was a newborn.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.260
Kaho was?

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:54.820
Right.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:08:00.830
I get that growing up in the red-light 
district must be rough, but still...

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.190
Indeed.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:06.670
She is a clever child and has figured 
out how to look after herself.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:11.240
But she can't remember her parents' 
names or what they look like.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.870
So even if she visited 
the Land of Memory,

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:17.600
she wouldn't recognize her 
parents or get to see them.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.830
Sosuke, you don't remember 
anything about your dad, do you?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.610
I don't remember anything 
before Otsuka Village.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.610
And I only vaguely remember 
my mother's face.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.780
But I think I still remember her.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:40.620
After all, she looked just like 
you. You even act the same.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.940
So don't you worry!

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:44.560
If we went to the Land of Memory,

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.900
I'm confident that at least 
I could find your mother!

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:50.380
Shino...

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:52.880
I'm goin' to sleep.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.740
Even if we made it there,

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:00.270
I don't care to see anyone 
in the Land of Memories.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.070
I have always...

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:09.150
...harbored but one wish.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.030
Hey! Kiddo!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.800
There ya are!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.160
Daikoku

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.720
I tried fixin' up that prototype!

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.470
I was hopin' you could try it out.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.850
Uh, okay?

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.560
Here's my curry bun with cheese!

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.820
Lemme see.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:32.530
You put in a whole quail egg!

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.200
Awesome!

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.280
If that's how ya feel, 
do ya think it'll sell?

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:40.800
Yup!

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.430
Since it was my idea, I wanna 
name it "Elegant Man Curry Buns".

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.430
ELEGANT MAN CURRY BUNS

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.980
That's hilarious!

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.220
The kimchee bun's good, too!

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.420
Really?

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.220
But I like dried shrimp 
and chives in my kimchee.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:58.510
What's next?

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.060
Chestnut and pumpkin?!

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.430
Make it less sweet and bring 
out the flavor of the chee-

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.900
Ah, stop right there!

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.460
I can't remember everything 
if ya tell me all at once!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.460
Could ya jot it down in this notepad?

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.270
Me?

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.810
It's a bit embarrassin', but I 
can't read or write worth squat.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.840
And while yer at it,

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.750
could you write down the 
recipes just as I tell ya?

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:25.850
What's the point if you can't read them?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.750
Don't you worry!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.200
I'll have Ma or my daughter read 'em.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.230
Okay, then.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.610
Here you go. I finished 
writing them out.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.260
Oh, much obliged!

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.120
Kiddo, I really appreciate it.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.640
Why are you acting so 
serious all of a sudden?

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.130
Well, thanks to you, I've 
got some new dishes!

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:52.660
I'll keep this nice an' 
safe in my family altar.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.250
Thanks again!

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.490
Now then, let's go back in.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:08.890
Mr. Shino, is there any way 
I could learn how to read?

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.460
If there's a book you want 
to read, I'll read it to you.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:14.970
Nuh-uh.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.900
I was wondering how 
you would read "Kaho".

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.290
Kaho, who gave you that name?

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.800
I don't know.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.570
They said it was on paper 
with me when they found me.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:30.910
Then it was probably your parents.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:40.420
KAHO

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:40.420
(?) The "Ka" in "Kaho" 
can mean "pretty person".

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.910
(?) The "ho" means "ear" 
as in "ears of rice".

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.410
You see it a lot in girl names.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.790
It's meant to be a 
blessing of fertility.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.440
Kaho

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:54.440
Wow!

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:56.590
Is that Kaho's name?

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.410
He said it means you're pretty!

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.940
You're so lucky, Kaho!

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.180
Hey, how about Goki?

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.010
Huh? Goki?

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:08.230
"Go" is referrin' to 
diamonds! Of all the nerve!

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:10.200
Really? Dang, I'm awesome!

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:12.480
I'm jealous!

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.940
Too cool!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.460
Do my name!

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.650
What's with this crap?

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.090
You can't see it anyway, 
so it's a waste of time!

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:26.850
What was that for?!

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.670
Even if I explained, I 
doubt you'd understand.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.600
It's a waste of time!

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.130
Shino!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.390
What's going on here?

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:50.660
It's nothing!

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.410
Let's go, Kaho.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.310
Come here.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.550
Sheesh!

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.990
What's a girl supposed to do

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:13.060
when the guy bursts into tears first?

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:29.950
DAIKOKUDO

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:29.950
Hello!

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.740
Welcome...

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:34.640
Excuse me!

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.350
When are you gonna release 
the old man's new menu?

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.840
What new menu...?

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.340
What? Was it still a secret?

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:45.280
He was goin' nuts taking notes 
for some secret recipes.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.280
Said he'd keep them safe 
in the family altar.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.740
Actually, I was the one 
who took those notes.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.510
Mom, the altar!

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.230
What the-?! Hey!

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.500
They're gone!

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.920
It's no big. I'll come back later.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:01.520
I wanna eat them now!

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.300
Good morning!

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.040
Hey, Sosuke!

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:11.990
Is it okay if I deliver those 
lunches sometime before noon?

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.040
Certainly. Thank you very much.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:17.610
Come to think of it, it's been 
a while since I've seen Shino.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:21.460
Lately he's been busy teaching 
the children at the church.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.500
Shino, teaching?!

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.410
Megu, don't you miss him?

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.760
I take it he hasn't been 
eatin' well, has he?

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:34.540
Actually, he has been receiving 
free food from Daikokudo every day.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.210
Shino has been loving it.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.780
Daikokudo? Why would 
they give him free food?

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:42.020
Apparently the owner 
knows Shino somehow...

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.500
Really?

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:48.280
But didn't the master of Daikokudo 
pass away a month ago?

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.750
Do you happen to know when

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.780
Shino befriended the good owner?

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.230
According to Shino, 
they were seeing each

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.290
other almost every day 
until about a week ago.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.900
But Daikokudo's new dishes have 
been extremely popular lately.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.300
Supposedly a line forms 
around the store every day!

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.800
I've heard about that! 
Elegant Man Curry Buns!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:10.320
Elegant Man Pork Buns     Curry Buns

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:14.910
Goodness, me! When Pa died, I had 
considered closing our doors.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:12.120
Korean Style

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.910
Super Man

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.310
Sorry, But We're Sold Out Super Man

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.660
Thank you very much!

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:19.970
But we couldn't close 
shop when he left behind

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:21.310
all those hilarious recipes!

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:23.810
Elegant Man Curry Buns and 
Super Man Sweet & Sour Pork!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.480
Daikokudo's Will Kihei Daikoku

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.480
I can just see him coming up 
with those names with that boy.

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.470
Mr. Sosuke, where is Mr. Shino?

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.250
He will be here later.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:45.880
Sosuke!

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:48.510
I finished passing out 
the sweet potatoes.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.110
Keno, thank you.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:54.890
Jeez! Those brats kept whining 
about which was bigger or smaller.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:58.120
And you put up with 
this all of the time?

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:00.710
But this was them on a good day.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:03.710
You see, a "beautiful lady" 
suddenly appeared to lend a hand.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.900
It made everyone tense up.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.300
You could have left out 
the "beautiful lady" part!

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:12.990
It looks like the last 
sweet potato is ready.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:16.370
Here!

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.060
Thank you, Mr. Sosuke.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:27.750
Didn't you say that child 
is completely blind?

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.120
She handles herself well.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:30.360
Indeed, she does.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.180
Her sharp senses compensate 
for her lack of vision.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.570
Sometimes she gives me a hard time.

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:36.790
How unusual!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:38.550
You should be able to handle a measly

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.430
brat if you throw around 
some of those phony smiles.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:45.220
Kaho can't see, so that 
doesn't work on her.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:47.990
Think about today. 
Unlike the other kids,

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:50.580
Kaho was the only one who ignored you.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:53.010
I happen to hate children.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:58.350
Right. Children can generally 
pick up on how adults feel.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:16:59.700
And that is especially 
true of that girl.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.710
Got it. I'll be careful.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.330
I'm not angry with you.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.480
It's just, Kaho instantly 
took a liking to Shino,

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.340
which I found rather puzzling.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:12.530
Hey, Sosuke!

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.340
Your hand!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.800
Doesn't that burn?

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.370
I can't say...

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.620
Since that day five years ago,

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:26.980
even if I get hurt, most 
wounds heal within a day.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.130
I had assumed that I was merely 
growing tolerant to pain...

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.020
But it looks like that isn't the case.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.490
Mr. Sosuke? Are you here?

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.000
Kaho? I'm here.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.050
The sisters are calling for you.

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.690
So you came looking for me?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.000
Thank you.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.990
Let's head on out. It's cold in here.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.460
He has a big, kind hand.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.310
But the palm of his hand is cold...

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:10.670
We have a special lunch today 
prepared by the people at Kona-ya.

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.830
It's incredible! So Kona-ya made this?

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.120
Why? What's up?

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:16.930
The innkeeper at Kona-ya and 
Mr. Shino are good friends,

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.910
so he asked her to make 
this as a special treat.

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:22.600
This food is too good to waste 
on their immature palates!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.040
Atsushi and Kaho, congratulations.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:28.020
Aren't your birthdays this month?

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:32.800
And Mr. Shino is going 
to sing for you later.

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:34.160
I'm not gonna sing!

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:34.160
Congratulations!

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:34.800
Thank you!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.300
Won't that be fun?

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:37.700
Yep!

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.050
Did you hear what I just said, Sosuke?!

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:48.190
Does that mean "Happiness" is at home?

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:48.190
Hmm. Well, I'd say you've 
pretty much got it.

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:51.660
Kaho, are there any books 
you'd like me to read?

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:57.190
Blue Bird?! We just read 
this the other day!

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:02.950
But it's fun how the story changes 
a little each time you read it.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.080
Sorry 'bout that.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:09.950
"In the end, the two went back home.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.700
They never did find the bluebird."

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.730
"But they learned just how dazzling the

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:21.100
simple little things in 
their everyday lives were."

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:27.870
M-Mr. Sosuke told me to bring 
you each a slice of cake.

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.050
Thank you.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.010
H-hey!

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:39.950
Yeah?

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:43.370
How do you write my 
name?! It-it's Atsushi!

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.600
Atsushi!

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:54.320
ATSUSHI

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.060
It can also be read as "Tokushi".

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.030
Tokushi?

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:56.880
It refers to someone

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:00.170
with a strong heart who 
is kind and considerate!

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.530
What was that for?!

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.370
Your name is way too good for you!

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.390
Shut up!

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.220
The sound of wings... A birdie?

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:12.800
Is it the bluebird?

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.900
This punk isn't that nice!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.050
Bye-bye!

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.380
Later! Bye-bye!

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.990
Come back again!

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:25.890
Bye-bye!

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.160
Let's go, Kaho.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.890
Bye-bye! See ya!

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:30.160
Uh-huh...

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:36.320
Mr. Shino, what is the 
color "blue" like?

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:39.670
Blue, huh? It's the color of the sky.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.390
I wonder if blue is a gentle color...

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:48.680
Oops, sorry!

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:50.680
Are you all right?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.400
Huh? By any chance, are you blind?

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:59.090
You have the same voice as Mr. Sosuke...

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:01.190
Do you know Sosuke?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:02.950
What's your name?

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:05.790
Kaho.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.150
Yeah? It's a mighty powerful name.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.450
Who gave it to you?

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:15.090
"Kaho" didn't have any meaning

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.350
until Mr. Shino gave meaning to my name.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:19.800
Shino? I knew it.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:21.720
You should take good care of that name.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.290
It is a powerful talisman.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:26.470
Who are you?

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.080
Me? My name is also Sosuke.

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:31.720
But you may call me Ao for now.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:33.730
Ao...?

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.090
See you later, Kaho.

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:49.740
He has the same kind hand as Mr. Sosuke.

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:53.080
But his was warm...

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:41.020
Ignorance

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:29.010
Shino, I heard you're 
teaching at the church?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.140
It's boring dealing 
with all those brats!

00:23:31.140 --> 00:23:32.240
Would you rather teach adults?

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:32.760
What?!

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.260
As an adult, I want you 
to teach me so much!

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.910
Shino, teach me all about your personal-

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:40.490
Police, there's a pervert here!
